# A null `cstr` handed straight back to C, which is the path nothing guarded
# until panel 053 (CLAUDE.md §12: a Heroes program must not segfault).
#
# `to_str` on a null `cstr` was always safe — `hero_str_from_cstr` checks the
# pointer and panics with its own name. This is the other path, and it is the one
# `to_str` never sees: the value arrives from C and goes back to C without ever
# becoming a Heroes string, so nothing looked at it. Measured before the guard
# existed, under `--sanitize`: `AddressSanitizer: SEGV on unknown address 0x0`,
# inside libsystem, with no line of this program on the stack.
#
# A `strstr` that finds nothing is the smallest way to get one. The check the
# author *should* write is on the line below, and it is writable only because
# `nullptr` takes the type its context asks for — the other half of the same
# sitting. This case deliberately omits it, which is what makes it an abort case.
# Fixed defect: `docs/panel/053`, 2026-08-14.

extern "string.h"
    function strstr(haystack: cstr, needle: cstr) -> cstr

function main()
    print("before")
    # `strstr` returns NULL when the needle is absent, so one binding produces
    # the null and consumes it. `getenv` was the first spelling and it is
    # deprecated by MSVC — a warning the harness forbids, and a dependency this
    # case does not need.
    absent = strstr(haystack: "abc".cstr(), needle: "zzz".cstr())
    # The result is **used**, not discarded: glibc marks `strstr`
    # `__attribute_pure__`, so `_ = strstr(…)` is `-Wunused-value` on Linux and
    # not on Darwin — a warning the harness forbids, and one more fact about this
    # project that only two platforms together could have told it.
    if strstr(haystack: absent, needle: "y".cstr()) == nullptr
        print("unreachable")
